# Local development environment template. Copy to .env at the repo root
# (gitignored, never committed) and fill in real values.
#
# BEL_DATABASE_URL is BEL's ONE runtime configuration contract — Alembic,
# the CLI, Web, and the startup schema gate all consume this same URL.
# See docs/PERSISTENCE-MIGRATION-POLICY.md.
#
# A repo-root .env is a SOURCE-CHECKOUT DEVELOPMENT convenience only —
# both `bel` and `alembic` auto-load it (src/bel/infrastructure/
# env_bootstrap.py) when run from within this checkout, so plain `bel
# web` / `alembic upgrade head` work without manually exporting anything
# first. This is never a general production configuration mechanism: the
# loader only activates from a real BEL source checkout (identified by
# this repo's own pyproject.toml + alembic.ini existing together) and is
# a silent no-op for a packaged/production install, which must always
# receive BEL_DATABASE_URL from its own deployment environment instead.
#
# Precedence (highest wins): explicit `--database-url` flag > an
# already-exported process BEL_DATABASE_URL > this .env file's value >
# a controlled "BEL_DATABASE_URL is required" error. This file's value
# NEVER overrides an already-exported shell variable of the same name.
#
# Canonical form: postgresql+psycopg://USER:PASSWORD@HOST:5432/DATABASE
# A password containing reserved URL characters (@, %, /, etc.) must be
# percent-encoded (@ -> %40, % -> %25, / -> %2F, ...).
BEL_DATABASE_URL=postgresql+psycopg://USER:PASSWORD@HOST:5432/DATABASE

# Only needed for local/private cutover-backfill acceptance runs — see
# docs/PRIVATE-DATA-POLICY.md. Never a path inside this repository.
# BEL_PRIVATE_DATA_ROOT=/absolute/path/outside/this/repo
